ppy) and community contributors using the custom osu-framework. While retaining the core circle-clicking, taiko, catch, and mania gameplay rulesets of the 2007 original, osu!lazer introduces updated game mechanics, including slider end accuracy scoring, real-time score processing, cross-platform mobile parity, and a highly customizable user interface and HUD layout.\n\nBuilt to eventually replace the legacy stable client, osu!lazer features a built-in skin editor, an overhauled multiplayer architecture with custom room settings, extensive gameplay modifier customization, and native support across Windows, macOS, Linux, Android, and iOS. Player progression, beatmap downloads, and global leaderboards are integrated directly with the main osu! infrastructure.", "themes": [{"id": 1, "name": "Action"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/osu-lazer", "videos": [{"id": 192229, "name": "Game Intro", "video_id": "ut_SOreClcc", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ut_SOreClcc", "title": "what is lazer?", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/ut_SOreClcc/maxresdefault.jpg"}, {"id": 192230, "name": "Dev Diary", "video_id": "D7SZk8mU7Ww", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D7SZk8mU7Ww", "title": "you can earn pp", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/D7SZk8mU7Ww/maxresdefault.jpg"}, {"id": 192231, "name": "Guide", "video_id": "26qsFcKO_7M", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=26qsFcKO_7M", "title": "osu! setup guide", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/26qsFcKO_7M/maxresdefault.jpg"}]}